    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_1009",
      "reading_order": 1450,
      "section": "IEC versions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 56.55,
        "t": 540.695,
        "r": 122.54780000000001,
        "b": 528.419
      },
      "content": "IEC versions",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1010",
      "reading_order": 1451,
      "section": "IEC versions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.5697,
        "t": 520.9214000000001,
        "r": 551.0869,
        "b": 482.34440000000006
      },
      "content": "For IEC designed control panels, the below suggested cable sections are calculated according to 60364-5-52 electrical installations of buildings, part 5: selection and erection equipment, section 52: current-carrying capacities in wiring systems."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1011",
      "reading_order": 1452,
      "section": "IEC versions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.56970000000001,
        "t": 475.32090000000005,
        "r": 559.3654999999998,
        "b": 436.7439000000001
      },
      "content": "Standard conditions refer to loose copper conductors or multi-core cable with 70C PVC insulation in free air or on open cable trays (installation method C) at 30°C ambient temperature and operating at nominal voltage. The cables may not be grouped with other power circuits or cables."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_1012",
      "reading_order": 1453,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.56970000000001,
        "t": 428.9405000000001,
        "r": 235.29009999999997,
        "b": 416.76350000000014
      },
      "content": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1013",
      "reading_order": 1454,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.56970000000001,
        "t": 410.6893000000001,
        "r": 230.57550000000023,
        "b": 396.3563000000001
      },
      "content": "ambient temperature > 30°C."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1014",
      "reading_order": 1455,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.56970000000001,
        "t": 384.28930000000014,
        "r": 269.56830000000014,
        "b": 369.9563000000001
      },
      "content": "cables not grouped with other cables"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1015",
      "reading_order": 1456,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.56970000000001,
        "t": 397.4893000000001,
        "r": 559.8604999999998,
        "b": 383.1563000000001
      },
      "content": "cables in closed race way, conduit or trunking system (installation method B2) at 40 °C ambient temperature"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0335",
      "reading_order": 1457,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 225.95774841308594,
        "t": 358.1971130371094,
        "r": 423.1049499511719,
        "b": 212.19012451171875
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0335.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_1015",
      "next_block_id": "txt_1016",
      "image_hash": "e37b620db64b708d83dba91e59522e629696fd9ddc47607ef40c8ddd9cb0cd97",
      "width": 197,
      "height": 146
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1016",
      "reading_order": 1458,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 90.57,
        "t": 180.18100000000004,
        "r": 560.8397999999995,
        "b": 141.60400000000004
      },
      "content": "Fuse calculations for IEC are done according to 60364-4-43 electrical installations of buildings, part 4: protection for safety- section 43: protection against over current. Fuse sizes are calculated in order to protect the cable against short circuit. Fuse type aM is recommended but gG/gL is also allowed."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig_0336",
      "reading_order": 1459,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 519.30322265625,
        "t": 815.9812164306641,
        "r": 567.0625610351562,
        "b": 792.9509963989258
      },
      "image_path": "figures/figure_0336.png",
      "previous_block_id": "txt_1016",
      "next_block_id": "txt_1017",
      "width": 47,
      "height": 23,
      "image_hash": "b28a1d23de5124d82d6f84120acacff249829ec0e42f4c826059a188d93e4d2e"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1017",
      "reading_order": 1460,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 186.7499573,
        "t": 710.5711571,
        "r": 535.7449035600007,
        "b": 687.9464104
      },
      "content": "The voltage on the compressor terminals must not deviate more than 10% of the nominal voltage."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1018",
      "reading_order": 1461,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 167.37,
        "t": 688.0110571,
        "r": 571.1769091100012,
        "b": 631.0664104
      },
      "content": "It is however highly recommended to keep the voltage drop over the supply cables at nominal current below 5% of the nominal voltage (IEC 60204-1). If cables are grouped together with other power cables, it may be necessary to use cables of a larger size than those calculated for the standard operating conditions. Use the original cable entry. See section Dimension drawings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1019",
      "reading_order": 1462,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 186.7499573,
        "t": 630.6510571,
        "r": 546.4961852699995,
        "b": 585.4664104
      },
      "content": "To preserve the protection degree of the electric cubicle and to protect its components from dust from the environment, it is mandatory to use a proper cable gland when connecting the supply cable to the compressor. Local regulations remain applicable if they are stricter than the values proposed"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1020",
      "reading_order": 1463,
      "section": "Worst case conditions refer to:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 168.99,
        "t": 585.5310571,
        "r": 217.8754866200001,
        "b": 574.1864104
      },
      "content": "below."
    }
  ],
